title: Security & Defence
subtitle: The Judicial Forces, defence policy and the Senate Guard.
is-card: true
tags: senate_affairs
card-image: img/card_forces.svg
view-if: security_timer <= 0 and chair_security = "rc"
on-arrival: turn_actions += 1; security_timer = 3; last_card_timer = "security"
new-page: true

= Security & Defence Committee

The Caucus chairs the Security & Defence Committee.

- @judicials: Expand the Judicial Forces.
- @oversight: Bring the army under Senate oversight.
- @guard: Return the Senate Guard to the Senate's command.
- @navy: Shape the Navy's officer appointments.
- @audit: Audit defence procurement.
- @review: Review the Republic's defences.
- @easy_discard

@judicials
subtitle: −2 treasury. +1 Judicial Forces, loyal to the Senate.
choose-if: treasury >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The treasury cannot afford it.
on-arrival: treasury -= 2; judicial_forces += 1; judicial_expansion = 1; sec_relation += 2; hawk_dissent -= 3

New Judicial cruisers are commissioned, crewed by volunteers sworn to the Senate.

@oversight
view-if: not army_oversight and (clones > 0 or kamino_known)
subtitle: −1 political capital. A permanent Senate committee over the army's commanders.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and rc_in_govt
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital and a seat in government.
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.6, guild: 0.4, rim: 0.6, sec: 0.25, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.1, cis: 0.5}, true);
Q.ov_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Grand Army Oversight Act', Q.ov_vote);
if (Q.ov_vote >= 50) { Q.army_oversight = 1; Q.navy_loyalty += 10; this.achieve('oversight'); }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if army_oversight : The Grand Army will answer to a standing Senate committee, which has full access to the army's orders, contingency plans and Kaminoan contracts. ?][? if not army_oversight : The Chancellor's allies argue that "a war cannot be run by committee". The bill fails. ?]

@guard
view-if: not senate_guard_reformed
subtitle: −1 political capital. The Red Guards would answer to the Senate, not the Chancellor.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and rc_in_govt
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital and a seat in government.
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.55, guild: 0.45, rim: 0.55, sec: 0.35, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.05, cis: 0.5}, true);
Q.sg_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Senate Guard Restoration Act', Q.sg_vote);
if (Q.sg_vote >= 50) { Q.senate_guard_reformed = 1; Q.pal_relation -= 10; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if senate_guard_reformed : The Senate Guard returns to its ancient blue robes and to the command of the Senate itself. ?][? if not senate_guard_reformed : The Guard remains under the Chancellor's office. ?]

@navy
view-if: clones > 0
subtitle: +8 Navy loyalty to the Senate; the Security Bloc objects.
on-arrival: navy_loyalty += 8; sec_relation -= 4

The committee confirms a slate of officers known for their loyalty to the constitution. A few promising officers loyal mainly to the Chancellor, such as one Captain Tarkin, are passed over.

@audit
subtitle: −1 corruption; the Security Bloc is annoyed.
on-arrival: corruption -= 1; sec_relation -= 4; treasury += 1

The audit finds that the Republic has paid for the same frigate four times.

@review
subtitle: Free. The Hawks appreciate it.
on-arrival: hawk_dissent -= 3; judicial_forces += 0.1
